      ":question/id": "df356eaf-6e61-57d5-a6b9-0f0386234268",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-110517",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
