      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-312358",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\text{arccot }x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
