      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341104",
      ":question/problem": "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+arccotx$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+arccotx) \\\\  & =2+\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
