      ":question/id": "7ca226a1-3aaa-542c-bc08-eb209e0b2aa2",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}-3\\operatorname{arccsc}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The inverse cosecant derivative is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc}x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=2\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)-3\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe negative coefficient and the negative inverse cosecant derivative give a positive second term. This derivative is valid for $x>1$, the interior of the function's real domain."
    },
