      ":question/id": "fad14dae-b314-5780-86a8-6f9980b62e4e",
      ":question/problem": "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x-3\\operatorname{arccot}x$ at $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The inverse cotangent derivative is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate using the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(x)&=2-3\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2+\\frac{3}{1+x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope is the derivative at the specified input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=y'(1)&=2+\\frac{3}{1+1^2}\\\\\n&=2+\\frac{3}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
