      ":question/problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=-\\operatorname{arccot}x+2\\ln(1+x^2).$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, and differentiate the logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+x^2}+\\frac{4x}{1+x^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{4 x + 1}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$."
