      ":question/problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5\\operatorname{arccsc}x.$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc}x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, with the power rule for the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=2\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)+5\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x>1$."
