      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec}x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, with the power rule for the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=1\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x>1$."
